            <div xml:id="d455">

                <pb facs="0462" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg450"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.00/2566: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador to the Polish Government in Exile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Biddle</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">at
                        London</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-22T19:00:00-05:00">December 22,
                            1941—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Polish Series No. 31. Your Polish Series 54, December 15, 7 p.m. You may attend
                    meeting as a guest, without, however, associating yourself with the text of the
                    Declaration. It is our understanding that that is the basis for participation as
                    proposed by the allied Governments established in London and the basis on which
                    the British Government has agreed to take part.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
